# Apple HIG

Before changing chrome or UX, read `hig/SKILL.md` and the surface in
`hig/screens.md`.

- One filled primary per view; secondary is ghost
- System SF, no extra body tracking, no remote fonts
- Live zinc tokens only; no DESIGN.md brown in chrome
- Hairline grouping; shadows only on floating menus/tips
- Motion ≤200ms and off under Reduce Motion
- Semantic controls; catalog strings; no raw shortcut IDs as labels
- No fake Liquid Glass; no Cooper/Copper copy

Canonical files: `hig/`. Adapters must not diverge.
